.TH TX\-VERIFY 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
tx\-verify \- check a transaction (stdin; any format tx\-decode reads) against what you expect
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tx\-verify [\-\-chain C] [\-\-expect\-to ADDR]... [\-\-change ADDR]... [\-\-chain\-id N (required for EVM)] [\-\-max\-fee N] [\-\-allow\-warnings] [\-\-allow\-value\-with\-token] [\-\-policy FILE] < tx
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
.RS 2
  tx\-verify [\-\-chain btc|ltc|doge] [\-\-expect\-to ADDR]... [\-\-change ADDR]... [\-\-chain\-id N (required for EVM)]
            [\-\-max\-fee SATS_OR_WEI] [\-\-allow\-warnings] [\-\-allow\-value\-with\-token] [\-\-policy FILE]
.RE
.fi
\-\-policy FILE: offline policy file (docs/POLICY.md); its findings are added and its sha256 is reported.
EVM default fee cap: 0.01 ETH (same as tx\-sign); UTXO: no cap unless \-\-max\-fee.
Exit 0 and status "ok" only when every check passes; otherwise status "failed", exit 1.
.SH OPTIONS
See SYNOPSIS; this tool has no separate long\-option list beyond \-\-help.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
tx\-verify: check a transaction (stdin; any format tx\-decode reads) against what you expect.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success (JSON lines may still carry status fields such as done / no_candidates).
.TP
2
Bad input, unsupported shape, or tool\-reported failure (JSON status is the detail).
.TP
3
Refused on purpose (watch\-only, policy deny, human abort, missing confirmation).
.PP
Other nonzero codes are tool\-specific; always read the last JSON status line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
See recipes/ for end\-to\-end flows. Search for tx\-verify in recipes/*.md.
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It opens hostile wallet files and extracts secrets: run it only sealed and offline (./blocktools run).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, docs/getting\-started.md, recipes/README.md
